  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the 12 files needed to trace both sides of the contract:\n\n**FastAPI request validation chain**\n1. `fastapi/dependencies/utils.py` \u2014 `request_body_to_args`, `solve_dependencies`, `analyze_param`: how declared body params (single vs. embedded, nested models) get matched against the parsed JSON dict and validated field-by-field.\n2. `fastapi/routing.py` \u2014 `get_request_handler`: where `await request.json()` is called and Content-Type is checked before treating the body as JSON.\n3. `fastapi/_compat.py` \u2014 the Pydantic v1/v2 shim; `ModelField.validate` wraps `TypeAdapter.validate_python`, the actual Pydantic v2 validation entry point.\n4. `fastapi/encoders.py`, `fastapi/params.py`, `fastapi/exceptions.py`, `fastapi/dependencies/models.py` \u2014 `jsonable_encoder`, `Body`/embed/media_type field definitions, and `RequestValidationError` shape.\n\n**httpx request encoding chain**\n1. `httpx/_content.py` \u2014 `encode_request`/`encode_json`: plain `json.dumps()` on whatever object is passed, no Pydantic-aware serialization; sets `Content-Type: application/json` only when `json=` is used.\n2. `httpx/_models.py` \u2014 `Request.__init__`: Content-Type negotiation between explicit `headers=` and the auto-derived one from `encode_request`.\n3. `httpx/_client.py` \u2014 client-level `request`/`post` methods that funnel `content`/`data`/`json` into `Request`.\n4. `httpx/_types.py`, `httpx/_multipart.py` \u2014 type contracts for `RequestData`/`RequestFiles` and multipart encoding (relevant since FastAPI's `Form`/`File` params expect `multipart/form-data`, not JSON).",
